 has training log metrics\n201\t3. **plan002-b01 eval** — experiment still running\n202\t4. **plan001-s42 component_count_mean** — not in registry metrics (need to extract from eval output)\n203\t5. **plan016 eval** — experiment still running\n204\t\n205\t---\n206\t\n207\t## Priority Actions (ordered by impact)\n208\t\n209\t1. **🔴 CRITICAL: Run eval_sta.py on plan001-s43-r4 checkpoint.** Without this, 3-seed comparison violates C004. The s43 ISR=0 claim is currently unsupported by standardized evaluation.\n210\t\n211\t2. **🟡 HIGH: Run eval_sta.py on plan005 checkpoint.** Convex combination is a key Claim 2 data point. Training log ISR uses binary `_fast_fn`, unreliable for paper.\n212\t\n213\t3. **🟢 WAIT: plan002-b01 and plan016 complete + auto-eval.** These are running and should auto-trigger eval on completion.\n214\t\n215\t4. **⚪ DROP: plan006 Prolog.** Insufficient time. Downgrade Claim 3 to Future Work.\n216\t\n217\t---\n218\t\n219\t## Summary\n220\t\n221\t| Claim | Evidence Status | Gaps | Rating |\n222\t|-------|----------------|------|--------|\n223\t| C1: ISR as Hacking Diagnostic | 3 seeds done, ISR collapse documented, taxonomy exists | s43 needs eval_sta.py | ⭐⭐⭐⭐ |\n224\t| C2: GRPO Saturation | 5 conditions compared, ISR<random confirmed | plan005 needs eval_sta.py; b01/016 pending | ⭐⭐⭐⭐ |\n225\t| C3: Cross-Logic Generality | No evidence | plan006 not started | ⭐ (→Future Work) |\n226\t| ISR Boundary (Limitation) | Well-characterized null | None | ⭐⭐⭐⭐ |\n227\t\n228\t**Bottom line:** Claims 1 and 2 have strong evidence with two fixable gaps (eval_sta.py for s43 and plan005). Claim 3 should be dropped to Future Work. Two running experiments (plan002-b01, plan016) will strengthen but are not critical. The paper is writable with current evidence once the two eval_sta.py gaps are filled.\n229\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01WKkjJcBpt3wqMLPvAgtWiy","session_id":"efc1460b-26c5-437d-a8e2-f5f08210a763","uuid":"68e5df44-c083-463c-b3b0-3b737b238275","timesta