{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Azxa4sXK4GhKymixjhJpd8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both reviewers have completed their independent reviews. Now I need to proceed with the roundtable process:\n\nStep 1: Independent reviews ✓ (done above)\nStep 2: Cross-share — I'll share each reviewer's key points with the other\nStep 3: Convergence — synthesize areas of agreement/disagreement\nStep 4: Final consolidated report\n\nLet me synthesize the two reviews and produce the final report.\n\nKey points from R1:\n- Rating: 3/6 (Weak Reject)\n- Strengths: ISR formally clean, strong controls (random reward, SFT), ISR collapse trajectory compelling, premise-count-matched analysis honest, cross-seed diversity as finding, comprehensive ablation coverage\n\n\n- Major weaknesses: Model size discrepancy (1.7B claimed vs 4B used), imagined vs actual experiments concern, SMT-LIB 1 seed, incomplete hacking taxonomy (6 modes but only 3 defined), statistical insufficiency (n=11 vs n=21, no tests), no figures\n- Minor: Additive bonus not justified, 1000-step single seed, n=100 eval set small\n\nKey points from R2:\n- Rating: 3/6 (Weak Reject)\n- Strengths: ISR collapse is clean, meta-Goodhart well-evidenced, premise-count-matched is genuine contribution, cross-logic strengthens diagnostic claim\n- FT control well-chosen\n- Major weaknesses: Minimal algorithmic contribution (LOO not new), \"meta-level Goodhart\" rebrands standard Goodhart, severely underdeveloped related work (8 refs vs 25+ needed), \"first systematic study\" claim undefended, hacking taxonomy not positioned against existing ones\n- Minor: Single-seed results, coarse beta sweep, abstract overpromises\n\nBoth reviewers converge on the 3/6 rating, identifying the ISR collapse trajectory as the strongest finding while flagging the random-reward control as well-designed and the premise-count-matched analysis as valuable. They're unified in criticizing the inadequate related work, scattered single-seed results, and insufficient statistical rigor that undermines the paper's broader claims. Where they diverge is R1's emphasis on data integrity concerns versus R2's focus on limited algorithmic novelty and conceptual rebranding.\n\nNow I'm ready to synthesize these points into the consolidated report.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10521,"cache_read_input_tokens":58117,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10521},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"efc1460b-26c5-437d-a8e2-f5f08210a763","uuid":"8a24d0b4-d94b-499c-9477-04256ca462e5"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Azxa4sXK4GhKymixjhJpd8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"两位 Reviewer 独立审稿完成。进入 Roundtable 综合阶段。\n\n## Roundtable 综合\n\n**Step 2: 交叉分享** — R1 和 R2 的核心发现互补：\n- R1 聚焦实验完整性（模型规模标注、imagined experiments、统计效力）\n- R2 聚焦新颖性和定位（LOO 非新方法、\"meta-Goodhart\"概念膨胀、相关工作严重不足）\n- 两者在评分上一致（均为 3/6 Weak Reject），在多个维度上高度共识\n\n**Step 3: 收敛** — 统一评估要点：\n1. ISR 崩塌轨迹是论文最强结果（共识）\n2. 随机 reward 对照组设计合理（共识）\n3. 相关工作严重欠缺（共识）\n4. 许多实验为单 seed，统计检验缺失（共识）\n5. R1 提出的实验真实性疑虑（imagined experiments）是最严重的问题\n6. R2 提出的\"meta-Goodhart\"命名膨胀需要作者回应\n\n现在生成最终报告并提交。"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10521,"cache_read_input_tokens":58117,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10521},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"efc1460b-26c5-437d-a8e2-f5f08210a763","uuid":"34c54ea2-97fa-4adf-b975-736b206421d6"}
